  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## 12.4.1\n\n### Fixes\n- A fenced or indented code block inside a list item or a block quote shows only its code. Every line after the first also carried the list item's indentation or the quote's `> ` markers, and a fence indented by up to three spaces kept that indentation on its following lines, because the block's text was read as one span of the source rather than the lines the parser trimmed.\n- A code block whose first line is blank keeps its text instead of showing empty, and blank lines at the end of a fenced block are kept.\n- A `[` or `![` that opens no link or image is kept as text. It disappeared, so `[link [bar](/uri)` read \"link bar\" and `see [note` read \"see note\".\n- An HTML table split by blank lines keeps each part in its own HTML block. Markdown reads each part as a separate HTML block, and the cells of the later blocks were moved into a table after all of them, so the view showed them out of place and the written markdown repeated their text after the original HTML.\n\n### Behavioural changes\n- Lines in a code block are always separated by `\\n`. A code block read from a source with CRLF line endings used to keep the `\\r\\n`.",
